menu "Ego Link platform camera"

    config EGOLINK_PLATFORM_CAMERA_ENABLED
        bool "Enable bounded OV5640 single-frame camera seam"
        default n
        depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32S3
        help
            Opt-in engineering seam for the camera connector on the existing
            Waveshare ESP32-S3-SIM7670G-4G board. One call performs at most one
            init and one QVGA JPEG frame acquisition using one internal-DRAM
            framebuffer, returns the framebuffer, and deinitializes the
            driver. This deliberately leaves PSRAM disabled so the existing
            always-lock-free atomic invariants remain valid. Runtime internal
            heap headroom remains an unverified hardware gate. This does not
            enable commands, periodic capture, upload, or physical camera
            power switching.

    config EGOLINK_PLATFORM_CAMERA_SHARED_I2C_VERIFIED
        bool "Operator verified camera coexistence on shared platform I2C0"
        default n
        depends on EGOLINK_PLATFORM_CAMERA_ENABLED
        help
            The camera profile forces esp32-camera to its legacy SCCB driver
            and existing-I2C0 mode. platform_i2c_bus remains the sole bus
            installer/owner on GPIO15/16; camera deinit must not delete it.
            The historical camera smoke was camera-only, so keep this false
            until a joint image verifies camera capture plus QMI8658A/MAX17048
            continuity on the actual wiring. Capture fails closed while false.

endmenu
